WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.350
Will Ferrell might be one of the funniest
people on the planet.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.640
But even though he makes people laugh for
a living, he's not immune to the power of

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.630
his own jokes, especially when he and his
co-stars are improvising gags on the fly.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.520
So what makes the funniest star in Hollywood
laugh?

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.271
Here's a look at some Will Ferrell bloopers
that make us love him even more.

00:00:16.271 --> 00:00:19.070
A glass case of screw-up

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.000
One of the most quoted lines the classic hit
comedy Anchorman is the moment when, during

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.710
a breakdown in a phone booth, he shouts

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.480
"I'm in a glass case of emotion!"

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.250
But as this clip shows, it took him a while
to get there - and the mistakes were almost

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.620
as funny as the final take.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.260
"Drew, do it again?"

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.130
The other bloopers

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:50.340
How hard must it be to film a scene with Farrell
when he's in the middle of one of his stream-of-consciousness

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.640
improv moments?

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.930
In The Other Guys, dramatic actress Eva Mendes
found out the hard way just how difficult

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.730
comedy can be when you're playing the straight
man to one of the funniest guys in Hollywood.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:09.860
"Doctor said it was similar to operating on
a German shepherd when they have hip dysplasia."

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.460
It's just science

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.170
Part of Anchorman director Adam McKay's job
is to keep the jokes flowing.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.310
So when the improv slows down, he pitches
in with ideas to get his stars riffing - which

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.130
backfired spectacularly on the set of Anchorman
2 when he suggested a very unusual material

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.260
could be used for the filler in breast implants.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.120
"What else did I have…"

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:28.900
"Nickels."

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.000
And they just could not pull it together.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.660
"The problem they're running into now is whenever
a woman runs…"

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.820
This outtake is so hot right now

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:52.579
Before his breakout role in Old School made
him a Hollywood star, Will Ferrell spent his

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:56.659
time as a supporting actor stealing scenes
in other people's films - like when he played

00:01:56.659 --> 00:01:57.909
Mugatu in Zoolander.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:02.320
Luckily, he soon got his own movies, no doubt
thanks to moments like this one:

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.580
"Waaaah!

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.220
WAHHH!"

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.280
Hey, tantrums sometimes work!

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:13.960
Something extra

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.820
It's hard enough for superstar actors to keep
a straight face while working with Ferrell.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:21.010
Now imagine how hard it must be for extras!

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:25.209
Well, you don't have to imagine, as this slip
up on the set of Daddy's Home 2 had the whole

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:26.209
room breaking character.

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:29.159
"Look at here, she's standing on the, GIVE
ME A PHONE, GIVE ME A PHONE, GIVE ME A PHONE!"

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.640
"I don't have a phone, props never gave me
a phone!"

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.000
Talladega lunch

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.599
One of the best loved scenes in Talladega
Nights is the extended sequence where Ricky

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:43.430
Bobby's whole family gets together for dinner.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.599
"Chip, I'm going to come at you like a spider
monkey."

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:50.129
But co-star John C. Reilly loved it just a
little too much, as he couldn't quite keep

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:51.769
a straight face during filming.

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:54.460
"I sure as hell am, Chip.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.240
CHIP!"

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:02.719
Bloopers of glory

00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:06.840
The skating comedy Blades of Glory is a just
a minor entry in Ferrell's catalog of comedy

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.849
classics, but it sure looks like the cast
had a good time filming it.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:13.400
"Of course not."

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.680
"I shouldn't do the sound effect, eh?"

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.340
Ferrell and co-star Rob Corddry seemed to
have a particularly hard time keeping a straight

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.340
face together.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.809
"You smell like urine."

00:03:23.809 --> 00:03:29.739
"I would fire you if you weren't so goddamn
beautiful out there."

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:31.769
Behold the majestic wolf lamp

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:35.979
Step Brothers is the tale of enemies who become
family, and then become friends - just like

00:03:35.979 --> 00:03:39.519
Ferrell is clearly good friends with his frequent
co-star, John C. Reilly.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:43.530
Their camaraderie is on full display in this
ridiculous scene involving Ferrell's "majestic

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.530
wolf lamp:"

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.810
"This is Galco, which is Hebrew for 'kindness'."

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.320
"Galco?"

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.519
And it just kept going.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:57.079
"You can't put a name on the innocence of
that face."

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.159
Live, from New York

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:06.430
When you crack up filming a movie, you can
just film it again to get it right.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:10.719
But when you crack up on live TV, there's
not much you can do except go with it, as

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.200
Ferrell found out after having to introduce
Tim Meadows as "Dr. Poop."

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:22.300
"The truth is, we misplaced your baby."

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.740
And that's not the only time Ferrell cracked
during his time on Saturday Night Live.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.720
"We're going to the Dolce &amp; Gabana show.

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:35.800
How fast can you have your bags packed for
Milan?"

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.940
Keep on laughing, Will!

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.000
Thanks for watching!

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.190
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

